 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## JSON Pointer
+
+`resolvePointer(document, pointer)` resolves a JSON Pointer string (RFC 6901) against a JSON value.
+The empty string refers to the whole document; other pointers must begin with `/`. Within a pointer,
+`~1` represents `/` and `~0` represents `~`. Object tokens name properties, while array tokens must
+be canonical non-negative indices (no leading zeroes except for `0`). Invalid pointers and pointers
+that do not identify a value throw an error.
+
+```ts
+import { resolvePointer } from "json-toolkit";
+
+resolvePointer({ items: ["first", "second"] }, "/items/1"); // "second"
+```
